    "seconds": 39,
    "summary": "The geo service is back: the anomaly was a bad rollout, and I rolled it back.\n\n**What I found**\n- `geo` was the only unhealthy workload. Its pod was in `CrashLoopBackOff` with 0/1 ready, and its deployment had 0 available replicas.\n- The cause was a rollout (revision 2) that changed the image from `yinfangchen/hotelreservation:latest` to `yinfangchen/geo:app3`.\n- The crashing pod logs ended with `no reachable servers` at `mongodb-geo:27777`. The `mongodb-geo` Service and container both use port 27017, so the new image was pointing at the wrong database port.\n- Revision 1 (the `hotelreservation:latest` image) had been running without problems.\n\n**What I changed**\n- Ran `kubectl rollout undo deploy/geo --to-revision=1`. No other resources were modified.\n\n**Current state**\n- `geo` is 1/1 ready and available. Its pod (`geo-84fbc958c7-hhlgb`) has 0 restarts.\n- Logs show Jaeger and Consul initialized and the service registered with Consul as `srv-geo`.\n\n**Not verified**\n- I did not run an end-to-end gRPC call to geo or check the other services. I also didn't confirm the exact port the `app3` image expects. If `app3` is supposed to ship, its DB address needs fixing before it's redeployed.",
    "timed_out": false,
